# Elene backend configuration.
#
# This backend is NOT shared - every deployment (yours included) needs its own copy of this
# file with your own keys. The Android app has no built-in backend of its own; after you deploy
# this, paste your backend's URL into the app under Settings > Elene Backend > Backend URL.
#
# Copy this file to .env for local runs (`.env` is already gitignored, never commit your real
# one). On Cloud Run / another host, set these as real environment variables in that platform's
# dashboard/CLI instead of shipping a .env file with your container.

# ---- LLM providers (at least ONE of these four is required for /elene/chat to work at all) ----
# Tried in this order: OpenAI first, then Anthropic, then Groq, then OpenRouter, as a fallback
# chain - if you only want one provider, only set that one; leaving the rest blank is fine.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional override, defaults to a Haiku model if unset:
ANTHROPIC_CHAT_MODEL_CHEAP=
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Optional override, defaults to llama-3.1-8b-instant if unset:
GROQ_CHAT_MODEL=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional override, defaults to openai/gpt-4o-mini if unset:
OPENROUTER_CHAT_MODEL=

# ---- Text-to-speech for Elene's voice (optional - without this, the app falls back to the
# phone's own on-device system voice instead of a real ElevenLabs voice) ----
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# The specific ElevenLabs voice id to use:
ELEVENLABS_MALE1_VOICE_ID=

# ---- Email alerts (optional - powers Sequence Mode's "notify me" emails). Needs a Gmail
# account with an App Password (Google Account > Security > 2-Step Verification > App
# Passwords), NOT your real Gmail password. ----
GMAIL_USER=
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# ---- Self-update proposal pipeline (optional - powers the in-app Updates screen's
# fingerprint-approved "propose a change" flow, which files a GitHub issue a separate cloud
# agent polls for). Needs a GitHub Personal Access Token with `repo` scope on whichever repo
# you point GITHUB_REPO at - defaults to the original project's repo if you leave it unset,
# which is almost certainly NOT what you want for your own fork. ----
GITHUB_PAT=
GITHUB_REPO=your-github-username/your-fork-name

# ---- Phoenix Protocol backup bucket (optional - a Google Cloud Storage bucket used as a
# one-way backup destination for intruder-capture photos/location history right before
# Sequence Mode's own auto-wipe deletes them locally). Leave unset and the corresponding
# endpoint just reports itself unavailable instead of erroring. Needs a GCP project with a
# bucket already created, and this backend's runtime identity needs write access to it - on
# Cloud Run that's whatever service account the service runs as; elsewhere, set
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS to a service account JSON key file instead. ----
EVACUATION_BUCKET=
